From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 08:05:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: msm8998: vote the bus for the video codec

venus_runtime_resume() votes the bus before it powers the core, and the order
is deliberate -- the core cannot be reached otherwise:

	icc_set_bw(core->video_path, kbps_to_icc(20000), 0);
	icc_set_bw(core->cpucfg_path, kbps_to_icc(1000), 0);
	if (pm_ops->core_power)
		pm_ops->core_power(core, POWER_ON);

msm8998's video-codec node has never carried interconnects, and
devm_of_icc_get() returns NULL rather than an error when the property is
absent, so both votes are silent no-ops and core_power() then touches
registers on a path with no bandwidth. Wire the two paths the driver asks for
by name, mirroring the display subsystem in the same file.

This is a completeness fix, NOT a fix for bringing venus up, and the
distinction is measured rather than assumed. With the node enabled and this
patch applied, loading venus_core still kills the SoC instantly: netconsole --
verified end to end on two transports immediately beforehand -- carries the
marker printed one line earlier and then nothing at all, and the phone returns
on the hardware watchdog. Identical to the behaviour without it. So the
missing bus vote is real and worth fixing, but something else in the msm8998
venus bring-up is fatal, and the node stays disabled until that is found.

Do not enable the node on the strength of this patch. It bootloops the device,
and the only way out is a physical Power+VolDown into fastboot.

Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998.dtsi
@@ -4258,6 +4258,11 @@
 				 <&mmss_smmu 0x42d>,
 				 <&mmss_smmu 0x411>,
 				 <&mmss_smmu 0x431>;
+			interconnects = <&mnoc MASTER_VIDEO_P0 RPM_ALWAYS_TAG
+					 &bimc SLAVE_EBI RPM_ALWAYS_TAG>,
+					<&gnoc MASTER_APPS_PROC RPM_ALWAYS_TAG
+					 &mnoc SLAVE_VENUS_CFG RPM_ALWAYS_TAG>;
+			interconnect-names = "video-mem", "cpu-cfg";
 			memory-region = <&venus_mem>;
 			status = "disabled";
 
